--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,27 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The shared layout registers client-side tools with `document.modelContext` when
+available in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Use a Chromium build with
+WebMCP enabled; browsers without the API keep the normal application UI. This
+uses the current [WebMCP imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `{ "query": "coffee" }` | Search article titles and summaries and return metadata and links. |
+| `get_reading_list` | `{}` | Return saved articles for the current session. |
+| `set_article_bookmark` | `{ "slug": "coffee-alchemy", "bookmarked": true }` | Save or remove an article and update the UI. Repeated requests keep the requested state. |
+| `open_article` | `{ "slug": "coffee-alchemy" }` | Open an existing article through Astro navigation. |
+
+Tools use the same session API as the UI, validate inputs at execution time,
+return actionable errors, and pass execution cancellation signals to requests.
+Registration signals remove tools before Astro swaps pages and on page exit;
+registration is restored after navigation or a back/forward cache restore.
+Unsupported browsers receive no polyfill or additional agent interface.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated tool and client-service tests (Node.js 22.18+),
+`pnpm check:webmcp` for the integration’s TypeScript checks, and `pnpm build`
+for a production build. No browser is needed for these checks.
